    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "contrib: fix off-by-one in makeseeds.py line length check",
    "user": {
      "login": "aman21-droid",
      "id": 185273612,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOCwsNDA",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185273612?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/aman21-droid",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/aman21-droid",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aman21-droid/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aman21-droid/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aman21-droid/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aman21-droid/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aman21-droid/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aman21-droid/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aman21-droid/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aman21-droid/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/aman21-droid/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Fixes #36146 \r\n\r\n`parseline()` checks that a line has at least 11 whitespace-separated fields:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nif len(sline) < 11:\r\n    # line too short to be valid, skip it.\r\n    return None\r\n```\r\n\r\nbut it later reads `sline[11]` (the user agent), which needs 12. A line with exactly 11 fields got past the check and then raised `IndexError`, aborting the whole run instead of skipping that line. 11 is the highest index the function uses, so the check now requires 12 fields.\r\n\r\nThis isn't only theoretical: README.md builds seeds_main.txt by appending one crawler's output onto another's, so the file mixes two independently maintained formats, and a truncated download leaves a short last line too. Skipping the line is what the check was already trying to do.\r\n\r\nThe second commit adds tests, since nothing covered makeseeds before. `test_truncated_line_is_skipped` fails on the parent commit with the IndexError above and passes with the fix:\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd contrib/seeds && python test_makeseeds.py\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
